IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc3-helpers`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4, ss 60 to 62 (part ssc3).
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-1992-4.txt, a plain-text rendering by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- Failure to satisfy the contribution conditions (ss 60 and 60A), the exclusion of increases (s 61), contributions paid in
-- error (s 61A) and graduated retirement benefit (s 62). Sections 61ZA to 61ZC are in ssc3-a0-s61za-s61zc.l4.
--
-- Where the Act lets regulations decide a person's entitlement (ss 60(1), 60A(2), 61A(2)), the regulations are not among the
-- sources: whether they exist and what they prescribe arrive as inputs. A bare power to make machinery or to amend another
-- Act (ss 60(5), 61A(4) and (6), 62(1) and (2)) has no function here, and its coverage row in NOTES.md says inert (reason 2).

§ `Part II: failure to satisfy the contribution conditions`

§§ `Section 60: complete or partial failure to satisfy contribution conditions`

-- (9): references in section 60 to a Category A or Category B retirement pension do not include one to which paragraph 5A of
-- Schedule 3, Part I applies.
-- src:1816 | (9) References in this section to a Category A or Category B retirement pension do not include one to which Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A applies.
@ref s 60(9) (src:1816)
GIVEN `Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A applies to the pension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(9) the pension counts as a Category A or Category B retirement pension in section 60` MEANS
    NOT `Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A applies to the pension`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this section to a Category A or Category B retirement pension do not include one to which Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A applies" -- a flat negative

-- (8): subsection (2) only has effect where the employed earner's death occurred on or after 11 April 1988.
-- src:1815 | (8) Subsection (2) above only has effect where the employed earner’s death occurred on or after 11th April 1988.
@ref s 60(8) (src:1815)
GIVEN `the employed earner died on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(8) subsection (2) has effect` MEANS
    `the employed earner died on` AT LEAST (Date 11 4 1988)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) above only has effect where the employed earner's death occurred on or after 11th April 1988" -- "only"

-- (3): the benefits referred to in subsection (2) are a widowed mother's allowance, a widowed parent's allowance, a widow's
-- pension and a Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of section 48B or 48BB (paragraphs (a) and (bb) are blank).
-- src:1801 | (3) The benefits referred to in subsection (2) above are the following—
-- src:1802 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1803 | (b) a widowed mother’s allowance;
-- src:1804 | (ba) a widowed parent’s allowance;
-- src:1805 | (bb) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1806 | (c) a widow’s pension;
-- src:1807 | (d) a Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of section 48B or 48BB above.
@ref s 60(3) (src:1801-1807)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
      `the pension is a Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of section 48B or 48BB` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A applies to the pension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(3) the benefit is one of those referred to in subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF benefit EQUALS `widowed mother's allowance` THEN TRUE
        IF benefit EQUALS `widowed parent's allowance` THEN TRUE
        IF benefit EQUALS `widow's pension` THEN TRUE
        IF benefit EQUALS `Category B retirement pension` THEN `the pension is a Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of section 48B or 48BB` AND `s 60(9) the pension counts as a Category A or Category B retirement pension in section 60` (`Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A applies to the pension`)
        OTHERWISE FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (d) in NOTES.md): "The benefits referred to in subsection (2) above are the following" -- read as a closed list

-- (2): where an employed earner who is married or a civil partner dies as a result of a personal injury of a kind mentioned
-- in section 94(1) or a disease or injury such as is mentioned in section 108(1), and the contribution conditions are not
-- wholly satisfied, those conditions are taken to be satisfied for the entitlement of the widow, widower or surviving civil
-- partner to any of the benefits in subsection (3), subject to subsection (8).
-- src:1795 | (2) Subject to subsection (8) below, in any case where—
-- src:1796 | (a) an employed earner who is married or a civil partner dies as a result of—
-- src:1797 | (i) a personal injury of a kind mentioned in section 94(1) below, or
-- src:1798 | (ii) a disease or injury such as is mentioned in section 108(1) below, and
-- src:1799 | (b) the contribution conditions are not wholly satisfied in respect of the employed earner,
-- src:1800 | those conditions shall be taken to be satisfied for the purposes of the entitlement of the employed earner’s widow, widower or surviving civil partner to any of the benefits specified in subsection (3) below.
@ref s 60(2) (src:1795-1800)
GIVEN `the employed earner died on` IS A DATE
      `the employed earner was married or a civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 94(1) the personal injury is of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 108(1) the disease or injury is such as is mentioned in section 108(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the contribution conditions are not wholly satisfied in respect of the employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 60(3) the benefit is one of those referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(2) the contribution conditions are taken to be satisfied for the entitlement of the widow, widower or surviving civil partner` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): "in any case where (a) an employed earner who is married or a civil partner dies as a result of ... and (b) the contribution conditions are not wholly satisfied" -- a failed "in any case where" is read like a failed "if"; and "Subsection (2) above only has effect where" (s 60(8))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST (`s 60(8) subsection (2) has effect` `the employed earner died on`)
          , JUST `the employed earner was married or a civil partner`
          , `ssc3 helper any of`
                (LIST
                    `s 94(1) the personal injury is of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)`
                  , `s 108(1) the disease or injury is such as is mentioned in section 108(1)`)
          , JUST `the contribution conditions are not wholly satisfied in respect of the employed earner`
          , JUST `s 60(3) the benefit is one of those referred to in subsection (2)`)

-- (1): regulations may provide for persons to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance, a widowed parent's allowance, a
-- widow's pension or a Category A or Category B retirement pension in cases where the first contribution condition
-- specified for that benefit in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 is satisfied and the second is not. Ask this of a retirement
-- pension: would it be payable only by virtue of the regulations? (seam S22; the regulations are an input.)
-- src:1787 | (1) Subject to the provisions of this section, regulations may provide for persons to be entitled to any of the following benefits, namely—
-- src:1788 | (a) a widowed mother’s allowance,
-- src:1789 | (aa) a widowed parent’s allowance,
-- src:1790 | (ab) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1791 | (b) a widow’s pension,
-- src:1792 | (c) a Category A retirement pension,
-- src:1793 | (d) a Category B retirement pension,
-- src:1794 | in cases where the first contribution condition specified in relation to that benefit in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 to this Act is satisfied and the second contribution condition so specified is not.
@ref s 60(1) (src:1787-1794)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
      `regulations under section 60(1) provide for the person to be entitled to the benefit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5 the first contribution condition for the benefit is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5 the second contribution condition for the benefit is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A applies to the pension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(1) the retirement pension would be payable only by virtue of section 60` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF benefit EQUALS `Category A retirement pension` OR benefit EQUALS `Category B retirement pension`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in cases where the first contribution condition ... is satisfied and the second contribution condition so specified is not" -- a failed "in cases where" is read like a failed "if" (marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md); and subsection (9)
            `ssc3 helper all of`
                (LIST
                    JUST (`s 60(9) the pension counts as a Category A or Category B retirement pension in section 60` `Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A applies to the pension`)
                  , `regulations under section 60(1) provide for the person to be entitled to the benefit`
                  , `sch 3 pt I para 5 the first contribution condition for the benefit is satisfied`
                  , `ssc3 helper not` `sch 3 pt I para 5 the second contribution condition for the benefit is satisfied`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): this function asks of a retirement pension, and the benefits section 60(1) lists are more than that

-- Section 60 as a whole: a retirement pension would be payable only by virtue of section 60 if it would be only by virtue of
-- subsection (1) or only by virtue of subsection (2). Sections 61(2) and 87(2) ask it in that wide sense; sections 61(1)
-- and 87(1) say "section 60(1)".
GIVEN `s 60(1) the retirement pension would be payable only by virtue of section 60` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 60(2) the contribution conditions are taken to be satisfied for the entitlement of the widow, widower or surviving civil partner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60 the retirement pension would be payable only by virtue of section 60 as a whole` MEANS
    `ssc3 helper any of`
        (LIST
            `s 60(1) the retirement pension would be payable only by virtue of section 60`
          , `s 60(2) the contribution conditions are taken to be satisfied for the entitlement of the widow, widower or surviving civil partner`)

-- (4): regulations under (1) shall provide for the benefit payable by virtue of them to be payable at a rate less than the
-- rate that would apply had both conditions been fully satisfied (subject to (7)). The prescribed rate and the full rate arrive
-- as inputs.
-- src:1808 | (4) Subject to subsection (7) below, regulations under subsection (1) above shall provide for benefit payable by virtue of any such regulations to be payable at a rate, or to be of an amount, less than that which would be applicable under this Part of this Act had both of the relevant contribution conditions been fully satisfied.
@ref s 60(4) (src:1808)
GIVEN `the weekly rate prescribed by regulations under section 60(1) in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the weekly rate that would be applicable had both of the relevant contribution conditions been fully satisfied in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 60(4) the weekly rate payable by virtue of regulations under section 60(1) in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the weekly rate prescribed by regulations under section 60(1) in pounds`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the rate is prescribed by regulations that are not among the sources
    WHEN JUST prescribed THEN
        CONSIDER `the weekly rate that would be applicable had both of the relevant contribution conditions been fully satisfied in pounds`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the full rate is that of Schedule 4, which is not among the sources
        WHEN JUST full THEN
            IF prescribed LESS THAN full
            THEN JUST prescribed
            ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the regulations "shall provide" for a rate "less than" the full rate; a prescribed rate that is not less is outside what the text contemplates

-- (7): regulations may provide that where (a) a person is entitled by virtue of (1) to a Category A or Category B retirement
-- pension consisting only of the additional pension with no basic pension and (b) that pension and any graduated retirement
-- benefit together amount to less than the prescribed rate, the entitlement shall be satisfied altogether or for a prescribed
-- period by a single payment of the prescribed amount.
-- src:1811 | (7) Regulations may provide that where—
-- src:1812 | (a) a person is entitled by virtue of subsection (1) above to a Category A or Category B retirement pension consisting only of the additional pension with no basic pension, and
-- src:1813 | (b) that retirement pension, and any graduated retirement benefit to which he may be entitled, together amount to less than the prescribed rate,
-- src:1814 | that person’s entitlement as respects that retirement pension shall be satisfied either altogether or for a prescribed period by the making of a single payment of the prescribed amount.
@ref s 60(7) (src:1811-1814)
GIVEN `regulations under section 60(7) so provide` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the pension consists only of the additional pension with no basic pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate of the retirement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly rate of any graduated retirement benefit to which the person may be entitled in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed rate in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(7) the entitlement as respects the retirement pension is satisfied by a single payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the prescribed rate in pounds`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the prescribed rate is set by regulations
    WHEN JUST rate THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): "Regulations may provide that where (a) ... and (b) ..." -- a failed "where" is read like a failed "if"
        `ssc3 helper all of`
            (LIST
                `regulations under section 60(7) so provide`
              , JUST `the pension consists only of the additional pension with no basic pension`
              , JUST ((`the weekly rate of the retirement pension in pounds` PLUS `the weekly rate of any graduated retirement benefit to which the person may be entitled in pounds`) LESS THAN rate))

§§ `Section 60A: failure to satisfy contribution condition in paragraph 5A of Schedule 3`

-- (6): references in subsections (1) to (3) to the condition in paragraph 5A, or to the requirements of paragraph 5A(2)(a)
-- and (b), include that condition or those requirements as modified by virtue of paragraph 5A(4). Where paragraph 5A(4)
-- modifies them, the modified condition is the one applied (fork F7, see NOTES.md).
-- src:1828 | (6) In subsections (1) to (3) any reference—
-- src:1829 | (a) to the contribution condition in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A, or
-- src:1830 | (b) to the requirements of paragraph 5A(2)(a) and (b),
-- src:1831 | includes a reference to that condition or those requirements as modified by virtue of paragraph 5A(4).
@ref s 60A(6) (src:1828-1831)
GIVEN `paragraph 5A(4) modifies the condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition as modified by virtue of paragraph 5A(4) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the condition as unmodified is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60A(6) the contribution condition in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A is satisfied for the purposes of subsections (1) to (3)` MEANS
    IF `paragraph 5A(4) modifies the condition`
    THEN `the condition as modified by virtue of paragraph 5A(4) is satisfied`
    ELSE `the condition as unmodified is satisfied`  -- fork F7 (see NOTES.md): the text says the reference "includes" the modified condition; it does not say the unmodified one is dropped

-- (4): "the contributor" means the person by whom the condition is to be satisfied.
-- src:1821 | (4) “The contributor” means the person by whom the condition is to be satisfied.
@ref s 60A(4) (src:1821)
GIVEN `the person by whom the condition is to be satisfied` IS A Person
GIVETH A Person
`s 60A(4) the contributor` MEANS `the person by whom the condition is to be satisfied`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"The contributor\" means the person by whom the condition is to be satisfied" -- a definition that says "means"

-- (1): subsection (2) applies if the contribution condition in paragraph 5A is not satisfied in relation to a benefit to
-- which that paragraph applies.
-- src:1818 | (1) Subsection (2) below applies if the contribution condition in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A is not satisfied in relation to a benefit to which that paragraph applies.
@ref s 60A(1) (src:1818)
GIVEN `s 60A(6) the contribution condition in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A is satisfied for the purposes of subsections (1) to (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the benefit is one to which paragraph 5A applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60A(1) subsection (2) applies` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) below applies if the contribution condition ... is not satisfied in relation to a benefit to which that paragraph applies" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            `ssc3 helper not` `s 60A(6) the contribution condition in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A is satisfied for the purposes of subsections (1) to (3)`
          , JUST `the benefit is one to which paragraph 5A applies`)

-- (3): a year of the contributor's working life falls within this subsection if it is a year in relation to which the
-- requirements in paragraph 5A(2)(a) and (b) of Part I of Schedule 3 are satisfied.
-- src:1820 | (3) A year of the contributor's working life falls within this subsection if it is a year in relation to which the requirements in paragraph 5A(2)(a) and (b) of Part I of Schedule 3 are satisfied.
@ref s 60A(3) (src:1820)
GIVEN `the requirement in paragraph 5A(2)(a) is satisfied in relation to the year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirement in paragraph 5A(2)(b) is satisfied in relation to the year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60A(3) the year of the contributor's working life falls within this subsection` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A year of the contributor's working life falls within this subsection if it is a year in relation to which the requirements in paragraph 5A(2)(a) and (b) ... are satisfied" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            `the requirement in paragraph 5A(2)(a) is satisfied in relation to the year`
          , `the requirement in paragraph 5A(2)(b) is satisfied in relation to the year`)

-- (2): a person who would have been entitled to the benefit had the condition been satisfied is nevertheless entitled to a
-- prescribed proportion of the benefit in respect of each year of the contributor's working life that falls within (3).
-- The proportion is read as the prescribed proportion for each such year, times the number of such years (fork F8).
-- src:1819 | (2) A person who would have been entitled to the benefit had the condition been satisfied shall nevertheless be entitled to a prescribed proportion of that benefit in respect of each of the years of the contributor's working life that falls within subsection (3) below.
@ref s 60A(2) (src:1819)
GIVEN `s 60A(1) subsection (2) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person would have been entitled to the benefit had the condition been satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the number of years of the contributor's working life that fall within subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed proportion for each such year` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 60A(2) the proportion of the benefit to which the person is entitled` MEANS
    CONSIDER `ssc3 helper all of` (LIST `s 60A(1) subsection (2) applies`, `the person would have been entitled to the benefit had the condition been satisfied`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the condition is satisfied, or whether the person would have been entitled, is not decided here
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST 0  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who would have been entitled to the benefit had the condition been satisfied shall nevertheless be entitled" under (2), which applies only "if the contribution condition ... is not satisfied" -- a failed "if" counts as no entitlement under this subsection (marginal reading (a))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `the prescribed proportion for each such year`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the proportion is prescribed by regulations that are not among the sources
        WHEN JUST proportion THEN JUST (proportion TIMES `the number of years of the contributor's working life that fall within subsection (3)`)

-- (5): where an employed earner who is married or a civil partner dies on or after 6 April 2010 as a result of a personal
-- injury of a kind mentioned in section 94(1) or a disease or injury such as is mentioned in section 108(1), and the condition
-- in paragraph 5A is not satisfied in respect of the employed earner, that condition is taken to be satisfied for the
-- entitlement of the widow, widower or surviving civil partner to a Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of section 48B.
-- src:1822 | (5) In any case where—
-- src:1823 | (a) an employed earner who is married or a civil partner dies on or after 6th April 2010 as a result of—
-- src:1824 | (i) a personal injury of a kind mentioned in section 94(1) below, or
-- src:1825 | (ii) a disease or injury such as is mentioned in section 108(1) below, and
-- src:1826 | (b) the contribution condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A is not satisfied in respect of the employed earner,
-- src:1827 | that condition shall be taken to be satisfied for the purposes of the entitlement of the employed earner's widow, widower or surviving civil partner to a Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of section 48B.
@ref s 60A(5) (src:1822-1827)
GIVEN `the employed earner died on` IS A DATE
      `the employed earner was married or a civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 94(1) the personal injury is of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 108(1) the disease or injury is such as is mentioned in section 108(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A is not satisfied in respect of the employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pension is a Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of section 48B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60A(5) the condition in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A is taken to be satisfied for the entitlement of the widow, widower or surviving civil partner` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): "In any case where (a) an employed earner who is married or a civil partner dies on or after 6th April 2010 as a result of ... and (b) the contribution condition ... is not satisfied" -- a failed "in any case where" is read like a failed "if"
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST (`the employed earner died on` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 2010))
          , JUST `the employed earner was married or a civil partner`
          , `ssc3 helper any of`
                (LIST
                    `s 94(1) the personal injury is of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)`
                  , `s 108(1) the disease or injury is such as is mentioned in section 108(1)`)
          , JUST `the condition specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A is not satisfied in respect of the employed earner`
          , JUST `the pension is a Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of section 48B`)

§§ `Section 61: exclusion of increase of benefit for failure to satisfy contribution condition`

-- (1): a Category A or Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of section 60(1), and a widowed mother's allowance or
-- widowed parent's allowance so payable, shall not be increased under section 47(1) or under Part IV if the pension or
-- allowance contains no basic pension in consequence of a failure to satisfy a contribution condition.
-- src:1833 | (1) A Category A or Category B retirement pension which is payable by virtue of section 60(1) above and a widowed mother’s allowance or widowed parent’s allowance which is so payable shall not be increased under section 47(1) above or under Part IV below ... if the pension or allowance contains no basic pension in consequence of a failure to satisfy a contribution condition.
@ref s 61(1) (src:1833)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
      `the benefit is payable by virtue of section 60(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the pension or allowance contains no basic pension in consequence of a failure to satisfy a contribution condition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(1) the increase under section 47(1) is excluded` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF benefit EQUALS `Category A retirement pension` OR benefit EQUALS `Category B retirement pension` OR benefit EQUALS `widowed mother's allowance` OR benefit EQUALS `widowed parent's allowance`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be increased under section 47(1) above or under Part IV below ... if the pension or allowance contains no basic pension" -- the exclusion is made "if" both facts hold; the same answer excludes an increase under Part IV
            `ssc3 helper all of`
                (LIST
                    `the benefit is payable by virtue of section 60(1)`
                  , `the pension or allowance contains no basic pension in consequence of a failure to satisfy a contribution condition`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 61(1) names a Category A or B retirement pension, a widowed mother's allowance and a widowed parent's allowance

-- (2): where a person is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit at a rate determined under section 30B(3) and the
-- retirement pension by reference to which that rate is determined (a) would have been payable only by virtue of section 60
-- and (b) would, in consequence of a failure to satisfy a contribution condition, have contained no basic pension, the
-- benefit shall not be increased under section 47(1) or under Part IV.
-- src:1834 | (2) Where a person is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit at a rate determined under section 30B(3) above and the retirement pension by reference to which the rate of the benefit is determined—
-- src:1835 | (a) would have been payable only by virtue of section 60 above, and
-- src:1836 | (b) would, in consequence of a failure to satisfy a contribution condition, have contained no basic pension,
-- src:1837 | the benefit shall not be increased under section 47(1) above or under Part IV below ...
@ref s 61(2) (src:1834-1837)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit at a rate determined under section 30B(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 60 the retirement pension would be payable only by virtue of section 60 as a whole` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the retirement pension would, in consequence of a failure to satisfy a contribution condition, have contained no basic pension` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(2) the increase of the short-term incapacity benefit under section 47(1) or Part IV is excluded` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the benefit shall not be increased under section 47(1) above or under Part IV below" where (a) and (b) both hold -- a failed "where" is read like a failed "if" (marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md)
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            `the person is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit at a rate determined under section 30B(3)`
          , `s 60 the retirement pension would be payable only by virtue of section 60 as a whole`
          , `the retirement pension would, in consequence of a failure to satisfy a contribution condition, have contained no basic pension`)

§§ `Section 61A: contributions paid in error`

-- (1): this section applies to an individual if (a) they paid primary Class 1 contributions that, because they were not an
-- employed earner, were paid in error, and (b) prescribed conditions are satisfied.
-- src:1864 | (1) This section applies in the case of any individual if—
-- src:1865 | (a) the individual has paid amounts by way of primary Class 1 contributions which, because the individual was not an employed earner, were paid in error, and
-- src:1866 | (b) prescribed conditions are satisfied.
@ref s 61A(1) (src:1864-1866)
GIVEN `the individual has paid amounts by way of primary Class 1 contributions which, because the individual was not an employed earner, were paid in error` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed conditions are satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61A(1) this section applies in the case of the individual` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies in the case of any individual if" (a) and (b) -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            JUST `the individual has paid amounts by way of primary Class 1 contributions which, because the individual was not an employed earner, were paid in error`
          , `the prescribed conditions are satisfied`)

-- (3): the additional pension referred to in (2) is additional pension, calculated under section 45, for the individual or the
-- individual's spouse or civil partner for the purposes of a Category A retirement pension; a Category B retirement pension
-- payable by virtue of section 48B or 48BB; a widowed mother's allowance and widow's pension; a widowed parent's allowance;
-- and incapacity benefit (except in transitional cases).
-- src:1871 | (3) The reference in subsection (2) above to additional pension is to additional pension for the individual or the individual’s spouse or civil partner falling to be calculated under section 45 above for the purposes of—
-- src:1872 | (a) Category A retirement pension,
-- src:1873 | (b) Category B retirement pension for widows, widowers or surviving civil partners (payable by virtue of section 48B or 48BB above),
-- src:1874 | (c) widowed mother’s allowance and widow’s pension, and
-- src:1875 | (ca) widowed parent’s allowance, and
-- src:1876 | (d) incapacity benefit (except in transitional cases).
@ref s 61A(3) (src:1871-1876)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
      `the pension is a Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of section 48B or 48BB` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is a transitional case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61A(3) the additional pension is one to which subsection (2) refers` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF benefit EQUALS `Category A retirement pension` OR benefit EQUALS `widowed mother's allowance` OR benefit EQUALS `widow's pension` OR benefit EQUALS `widowed parent's allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF benefit EQUALS `Category B retirement pension` THEN (IF `the pension is a Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of section 48B or 48BB` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) names a Category B retirement pension "for widows, widowers or surviving civil partners (payable by virtue of section 48B or 48BB)"
        IF benefit EQUALS `long-term incapacity benefit` OR benefit EQUALS `short-term incapacity benefit` THEN (IF `the case is a transitional case` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "incapacity benefit (except in transitional cases)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the list introduced by "for the purposes of" does not say "only"

-- (2): regulations may, where this section applies and the Inland Revenue are of the opinion that it is appropriate, provide
-- for entitlement to, and the amount of, additional pension to be determined as if the individual had been an employed earner
-- and the contributions had been properly paid. The regulations are an input.
-- src:1867 | (2) Regulations may, where—
-- src:1868 | (a) this section applies in the case of any individual, and
-- src:1869 | (b) the Inland Revenue are of the opinion that it is appropriate for the regulations to apply to the individual,
-- src:1870 | provide for entitlement to, and the amount of, additional pension to be determined as if the individual had been an employed earner and, accordingly, those contributions had been properly paid.
@ref s 61A(2) (src:1867-1870)
GIVEN `s 61A(1) this section applies in the case of the individual` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Inland Revenue are of the opinion that it is appropriate for the regulations to apply to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations under section 61A(2) so provide` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61A(2) the contributions are treated as properly paid, as if the individual had been an employed earner, for the additional pension` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, read through marginal reading (a2) in NOTES.md): "Regulations may, where (a) this section applies ... and (b) the Inland Revenue are of the opinion that it is appropriate" -- a failed "where" is read like a failed "if"
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            `s 61A(1) this section applies in the case of the individual`
          , JUST `the Inland Revenue are of the opinion that it is appropriate for the regulations to apply to the individual`
          , `regulations under section 61A(2) so provide`)

-- (5): where such provision as is mentioned in (2) or (4) applies, regulations under paragraph 8(1)(m) of Schedule 1 may
-- not require the amounts paid by way of primary Class 1 contributions to be repaid.
-- src:1881 | (5) Where such provision made by regulations as is mentioned in subsection (2) or (4) above applies in respect of any individual, regulations under paragraph 8(1)(m) of Schedule 1 to this Act may not require the amounts paid by way of primary Class 1 contributions to be repaid.
@ref s 61A(5) (src:1881)
GIVEN `such provision made by regulations as is mentioned in subsection (2) or (4) applies in respect of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61A(5) regulations under paragraph 8(1)(m) of Schedule 1 may require the amounts to be repaid` MEANS
    IF `such provision made by regulations as is mentioned in subsection (2) or (4) applies in respect of the individual`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "regulations under paragraph 8(1)(m) of Schedule 1 to this Act may not require the amounts paid by way of primary Class 1 contributions to be repaid" -- a flat negative
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is made "Where such provision ... applies"

§§ `Section 62: graduated retirement benefit`

-- (4): "relevant gender change case", for a woman and her late wife, means a case where (a) the late wife was, at the time of
-- her death, a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate and (b) the marriage subsisted before the
-- certificate was issued.
-- src:1909 | (4) For that purpose “relevant gender change case”, in relation to a woman (“the pensioner”) and her late wife, means a case where—
-- src:1910 | (a) the late wife was, at the time of her death, a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004, and
-- src:1911 | (b) the marriage of the pensioner and her late wife subsisted before the time when the certificate was issued.
@ref s 62(4) (src:1909-1911)
GIVEN `the late wife was at the time of her death a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the marriage of the pensioner and her late wife subsisted before the time when the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 62(4) the case is a relevant gender change case` MEANS
    `the late wife was at the time of her death a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004`
    AND `the marriage of the pensioner and her late wife subsisted before the time when the certificate was issued`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"relevant gender change case\" ... means a case where (a) ... and (b) ..." -- a definition that says "means"

-- (3): in relevant gender change cases, women and their late wives are treated for the purposes of sections 36 and 37 of the
-- National Insurance Act 1965 in the same way as women and their late husbands.
-- src:1908 | (3) In relevant gender change cases, women and their late wives are to be treated for the purposes of sections 36 and 37 of the National Insurance Act 1965 in the same way as women and their late husbands.
@ref s 62(3) (src:1908)
GIVEN `s 62(4) the case is a relevant gender change case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62(3) the woman and her late wife are treated in the same way as a woman and her late husband for sections 36 and 37 of the National Insurance Act 1965` MEANS
    IF `s 62(4) the case is a relevant gender change case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the equal treatment is made "In relevant gender change cases"; sections 36 and 37 of the 1965 Act are not among the sources
